The  driver  provides  support  for the Sun Microsystems Bus Con‐
troller chipset found on various VME boards and on  the  Multibus
board.   All versions of this driver can be configured with a di‐
rective in the file.  The values are bits in a bitfield, and  are
interpreted  as  follows:  Set  bit (1<<target) to disable parity
checking Set this bit to disable interrupts (poll) Set  this  bit
to  disable  entirely (use PIO) For example: would disable inter‐
rupts, and disable parity checking for targets 0‐7.  The  is  the
ID  number  of  a  particular  device  on a particular bus.  This
chipset is rumored to have bugs in its handling of parity, there‐
fore it is recommended that you disable  parity  on  all  devices
connected to this controller, and configure it with a 0x0ff value
for  its  directive in the file.  This chipset has no support for
raising the signal, so there is no way to ever schedule  a  phase
on  the bus.  Currently, the driver will ultimately reset the bus
if this phase is ever requested by the upper layer driver.   This
chipset  has no support for disconnect/reselect.  This means that
slow devices, such as tape drives, can  hog,  or  the  SCSI  bus.
This  driver has not been tested in combination with non‐SCSI de‐
vices behind or bridges, which are common in 2s and  in  Shoebox‐
type  configurations.  These devices pre‐date the spec, and might
not behave the way the chipset code currently expects.
